# FEX's x86_64 + i386 ArchLinux RootFS: the "graphics provider" Valve's FEX tool needs to give x86
# Steam games and x86 Protons a GPU driver.
#
# Read by /usr/lib/retroforge/steam-x86-guest, which /usr/bin/steam starts in the background: it
# downloads the image into the player's home (~/.local/share/retroforge/fex-guest/<name>-<version>.sqsh),
# checks it, and the wrapper mounts it with squashfuse on ~/.local/share/retroforge/fex-guest/root
# while Steam runs. STEAM_COMPAT_GRAPHICS_PROVIDER points at root/graphics_provider.json, so that tree
# is both pressure-vessel's graphics provider and FEX's RootFS (docs/steam-arm64.md).
#
# Not in the image: it is 1.36 GB, a root slot is 2 GB (image/partition-table.txt), and
# rootfs/guard-rootfs.sh section 9 keeps x86 out of the root. SteamOS's own provider
# (/usr/share/guestos/fex-mesa, Valve's deckard-mesa-linux-x86_64) is the same kind of tree.
#
# A CHANNEL, not a version. Every `steam` start reads FEX's links file (one 5 kB GET, in the background,
# 15 s at most) and takes what its entry names now:
#   channel: FEX's RootFS_links.json, the file FEXRootFSFetcher reads. Its shape:
#            {"v1": {"ArchLinux (SquashFS)": {"DistroMatch": "arch", "DistroVersion": "rolling",
#             "Type": "squashfs", "URL": ".../ArchLinux/<date>/ArchLinux.sqsh", "Hash": "<xxh3>"}, ...}}
#   distro, type: the entry's DistroMatch and Type. Exactly one entry has to match; FEX lists one per
#            rolling distro and type, its newest. Two would be refused, not guessed between.
# The image is checked against the entry's Hash, an XXH3-64 in hex without leading zeros (FEX's
# XXFileHash: XXH3_64bits, seed 0), with xxhsum -H3 (package xxhash, in PKGS). A new image becomes
# current only once it is complete and checked; until then the one installed is used and mounted, and
# it is removed only once it is not mounted. Offline, or a links file that does not parse to one such
# entry: nothing changes. The file is named <name>-<dated directory>-<xxh3>.sqsh.
#
# Checked on 2026-10-16, ArchLinux (SquashFS): .../ArchLinux/2026-08-11/ArchLinux.sqsh, Hash
# 23350f949fc1413d, 1,359,826,944 bytes, squashfs 4.0, zstd. The image's own xxhsum (xxhash 0.8.3-1 from
# rootfs/manifest.lock) gives XXH3_23350f949fc1413d for it. graphics_provider.json is at its root
# (x86_64-linux-gnu: /usr/lib, i386-linux-gnu: /usr/lib32); usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/
# freedreno_icd.{x86_64,i686}.json point at /usr/lib{,32}/libvulkan_freedreno.so (Mesa 26.2.0); glibc
# with usr/lib/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 and usr/lib32/ld-linux.so.2. A later image FEX publishes is used
# without that check: whether x86 games keep working depends on FEX keeping those paths.
#
# A FIXED image instead (an image of our own, say): replace channel, distro and type with
#   version: <version>
#   url: <url>
#   sha256: <sha256>
# Then the image is checked against the sha256, and a new version downloads when this pin changes.
name: fex-rootfs-archlinux
channel: https://rootfs.fex-emu.gg/RootFS_links.json
distro: arch
type: squashfs
